00:05:02.184 --> 00:05:06.054
Now hair is very much affected
by the softness of water.

00:05:08.891 --> 00:05:13.929
But instead of me showing
you lots of pictures of hair

00:05:13.929 --> 00:05:19.401
that I found randomly on the
internet, googling soft water,

00:05:19.401 --> 00:05:23.405
hard water, different
forms of water, hair,

00:05:23.405 --> 00:05:26.642
I'm showing you pipes, because
that's much more actually

00:05:26.642 --> 00:05:29.111
relevant in terms of like, for
example, whether you can get

00:05:29.111 --> 00:05:31.513
water into your house at all.

00:05:31.513 --> 00:05:32.414
All right?

00:05:32.414 --> 00:05:35.150
And this is a real problem.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.985
If you have hard
water what it means

00:05:36.985 --> 00:05:40.022
is you've got
minerals in the water.

00:05:40.022 --> 00:05:40.756
Right?

00:05:40.756 --> 00:05:44.593
Things like magnesium and
calcium ions are in the water.

00:05:44.593 --> 00:05:48.530
And what happens is, if you run
that through pipes, they tend

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:52.601
to react and form and deposit.

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:55.170
And you get these deposits
of very, very hard mineral

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:58.373
deposits around the edges that
eventually look like this.

00:05:58.373 --> 00:06:00.075
That's not a good thing.

00:06:00.075 --> 00:06:03.612
And so you need to soften the
water, and that's something

00:06:03.612 --> 00:06:05.113
you may have heard of.

00:06:05.113 --> 00:06:07.516
But now you really know how
to think about it, because you

00:06:07.516 --> 00:06:09.585
can think about it in
terms of all of the things

00:06:09.585 --> 00:06:12.054
that you've learned.

00:06:12.054 --> 00:06:16.592
And just as an example,
if one of those minerals

00:06:16.592 --> 00:06:18.627
that's a problem is calcium--

00:06:18.627 --> 00:06:20.195
oh, it is, right?

00:06:20.195 --> 00:06:25.400
Magnesium is another one
that can cause this in pipes.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.971
You've got to somehow
take it out of the water

00:06:28.971 --> 00:06:33.842
or at least make it into a form
that makes it like insoluble,

00:06:33.842 --> 00:06:36.311
so it'll just flow, and
it won't have a chance

00:06:36.311 --> 00:06:41.617
to come around and deposit on
the edge there of the pipe.

00:06:41.617 --> 00:06:42.718
And so what do you do?

00:06:42.718 --> 00:06:45.220
Well, you add, for example--

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:46.788
oh, we've done this before.

00:06:46.788 --> 00:06:47.289
Right?

00:06:47.289 --> 00:06:51.293
What if I add soda,
something called soda ash?

00:06:51.293 --> 00:06:52.928
Oh, we know what that is.

00:06:52.928 --> 00:07:01.403
That's Na2CO3, and that
will give me some ions.

00:07:01.403 --> 00:07:04.172
It'll give me some
Na pluses, and it'll

00:07:04.172 --> 00:07:09.645
give me some CO3 2 minuses,
and those are in aqueous.

00:07:09.645 --> 00:07:11.280
Now, this is all
part of the stuff

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.514
that we've been talking about.

00:07:12.514 --> 00:07:14.950
You're dissociating this
to get ions in solution,

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:18.287
but why do I want these ions?

00:07:18.287 --> 00:07:20.022
That's a water softener.

00:07:20.022 --> 00:07:20.589
Why?

00:07:20.589 --> 00:07:22.157
Because now you can see it.

00:07:22.157 --> 00:07:22.658
Right?

00:07:22.658 --> 00:07:26.061
Because this one
here, this one here

00:07:26.061 --> 00:07:29.498
is going to remove the calcium.

00:07:29.498 --> 00:07:31.867
So if I've got these
calcium, these minerals,

00:07:31.867 --> 00:07:35.904
in the water making it hard
water which leads to that

00:07:35.904 --> 00:07:40.108
and wreaks havoc on
your hair, then you

00:07:40.108 --> 00:07:41.909
get a little of this
in there, and you're

00:07:41.909 --> 00:07:43.312
going to react with the calcium.

00:07:43.312 --> 00:07:43.812
Why?

00:07:43.812 --> 00:07:45.781
It's because of
what we already saw.

00:07:45.781 --> 00:07:47.749
If I have this--

00:07:47.749 --> 00:07:50.919
this is something we've already
looked at-- if I have calcium 2

00:07:50.919 --> 00:07:54.056
plus, and I have some
bicarbonate in there,

00:07:54.056 --> 00:08:00.562
CO3 minus, then we know that
I can get precipitates, Ca--

00:08:00.562 --> 00:08:03.065
this is just what we looked
at in the goody bag, right--

00:08:03.065 --> 00:08:07.469
plus CO2 plus H2O.

00:08:07.469 --> 00:08:10.973
That's the same kind of reaction
that we looked at already.

00:08:10.973 --> 00:08:14.109
We have calcium carbonate,
calcium carbonate.

00:08:14.109 --> 00:08:14.710
Why?

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:18.246
Well, because this is
going to give me these.

00:08:18.246 --> 00:08:23.485
This is a source for those
which then eats up some calcium.

00:08:23.485 --> 00:08:28.156
And you think, well, now this
can take the calcium ions out,

00:08:28.156 --> 00:08:30.525
so that it runs through.

00:08:30.525 --> 00:08:32.159
That's what you want to do here.

00:08:32.159 --> 00:08:34.229
That's how you soften water.

00:08:34.229 --> 00:08:38.100
Well, you can add lime which
gives me a source of OH minus,

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.501
and that takes
out the magnesium.

00:08:40.501 --> 00:08:43.038
And these are ways to change
the chemistry of water,

00:08:43.038 --> 00:08:46.008
so that you don't have
as many ions, mineral,

00:08:46.008 --> 00:08:49.344
these calcium and magnesium
ions floating around that cause

00:08:49.344 --> 00:08:50.712
